+/*
+ * THOR WITNESS V235 (Thor port only; included once, at the end of osfmk/kern/debug.c).
+ *
+ * v233 made a freeze leave evidence that does not depend on the UI: the panic log on the panel,
+ * a kernel-side hang report, and a kernel-side console mirror.  The first v233 run then showed
+ * what the "画面定格" is: a kernel panic ("Kernel Instruction fetch abort", backboardd, after 100
+ * minutes).  A photographed panic log leaves the decisive questions open: who called the bad
+ * address, what the thread was doing, and what the driver did just before.  So v234:
+ *
+ *   1. keeps the panic log and the hang report on the panel;
+ *   2. adds panic extras to the panel and to a record: the faulting pc/lr with their
+ *      translation, the bytes around them, the user registers of the thread, every kernel-text
+ *      word on the thread's kernel stack with its symbol, and the tail of the GPU trace ring;
+ *   3. stores the panic log and the extras in a pre-allocated file, written straight to the
+ *      storage blocks through the UFS driver (bsd/kern/kern_exec.c owns the slot).
+ *
+ * The only v234 run (2026-11-25, six minutes) lost the record twice over: the slot was never
+ * proven (kern_exec.c: the block numbers count from a partition 1 MiB into the window), and the
+ * GPU trace was read into a 24-byte object and ran 19 KiB past it into other kernel data.  Of the
+ * panel only one page was photographed: a list of kernel-text words, which cannot tell a live
+ * frame from a stale one.  So v235:
+ *
+ *   1. fixes both (the slot origin in kern_exec.c; one buffer for the GPU trace here);
+ *   2. adds two real backtraces to the extras: the frame records from the faulting code's frame
+ *      pointer (who leads to the fault), and the frame records at the panic call (who panicked).
+ *
+ * The monitor thread never waits for a contended lock and never touches storage; only the
+ * console mirror thread (kern_exec.c) does I/O while the system runs.
+ */
+#ifndef _KERN_THOR_WITNESS_V235_H_
+#define _KERN_THOR_WITNESS_V235_H_
+
+#define _KERN_THOR_WITNESS_V233_H_
+#define _KERN_THOR_WITNESS_V234_H_
